# Banked bench outputs — a machine-local cache keyed by content hash, and bulk
# model prose besides. The verdicts and their cited rationale live in the
# committed tests/bench/battles.jsonl; commit these too if cross-machine
# re-judging ever becomes a thing worth paying git weight for.
tests/bench/outputs/

# Everything `openspec init plans/development` generates: it writes the same six
# workflows twice for every tool it targets — once as a skill, once as a slash
# command — so four tools produced 42 files carrying six workflows. All of it is
# local tooling and is regenerated by re-running that init.
#
# What is NOT ignored, and must not be: the store itself, under
# plans/development/openspec/. Those specs and changes are authored, nothing
# regenerates them, and pr-shepherd, product-inception and openspec-conformance
# all reference the store by path — pr-shepherd gates on config.yaml existing.
#
# Deliberately narrow in two places: .claude/skills/two-store-memory-setup is a
# symlink into skills/ and stays tracked, and .opencode/commands/ also holds 59
# bmad-* files that are not OpenSpec's.
.agents/skills/
.claude/commands/opsx/
.claude/skills/openspec-*/
.gemini/commands/opsx/
.gemini/skills/
.opencode/commands/opsx-*.md
.opencode/skills/
